overflow in sub at i64

The one `k` at which the lag family is not defined. `out[i] = xs[i - k]`, and
`i - k` overflows i64 at `k = i64::MIN`, so `shift`, `shift_fill`,
`shift_clamped`, `diff` and `pct_change` all trap there rather than returning a
series. Every other `k` is defined: a negative `k` is pandas' lead, `k = 0` is
the identity, and any other out-of-range offset is reported as absence or as
the caller's fill rather than as a trap. The failure is loud, which is why the
docs state the limit rather than the module widening the index type.
